      {
        "id": 263238,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-05-18T17:24:13.248Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"31551\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So this might mean that they’ll do more print runs of already-published products?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Theoretically, but Branch &amp; Claw came out in 2017, and if there’s one thing I can say for sure about Spirit Island it’s that availability of products has been wildly uneven for years.  I don’t think there’s been occasion in the 2020s where I’ve gone to the FLGS and they’ve had everything in stock for it despite their best efforts to do so.  The owner’s constantly complaining about the range being hard to stock  and distribution being out of it, and that can’t be getting any better with the current situation.</p>\n<p>I mean, just look at the disparities between “have” and “want” on the BGG pages for the stuff.  Those kind of numbers are not the kind you see for games where the publisher is keeping up with production smoothly.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Sora\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"31551\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/sora/48/7084_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Sora:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’ve not heard of boardgamegeek before so I will have a look through that, thank you <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Oh dear, I may have sent you to a rabbit hole…nay, rabbit warren you may never escape from if you’re a fan of boardgames.  It’s quite a stunning database over there.  Have fun…but budget wisely, I guess?</p>",
